# CQ12 / neutrality (INHABITED-COMPETENCY.md, INHABITED-TRADITIONS.md): a
# CONTESTED inhabitation MUST NOT appear as a base-graph relationship. The
# possession fixture carries the lwa-mounts-horse relation ONLY inside an
# gmeow:InhabitationClaim's quoted gmeow:InhabitationDescription (range-open
# gmeow:describedSubject / gmeow:describedHost), so the asserted base graph is
# silent on the metaphysics — no gmeow:inhabitationSubject / gmeow:inhabitedHost
# edge and no gmeow:InhabitationTenure individual. This ASK MUST return false
# (gmeow:cqExpectAsk false); a true would mean the contest leaked into the base
# graph and (range gmeow:Agent / gmeow:Entity) would globally infer the spirit's
# type, collapsing the frame-neutrality Principle 9 requires.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    { ?s gmeow:inhabitationSubject ?o }
    UNION { ?s gmeow:inhabitedHost ?o }
    UNION { ?t a gmeow:InhabitationTenure }
}
